>My cabinet is a BA215
The cable from a BA213 should also work.

In the BA440 cabinet the DSSI bus is built into the backplane
behind the DSSI drives.  The only thing the cable does is
connect the back plane to the external connector, and it has
one internal and one external connector.

Your best hope is to find some dealer who has "parted out" a
BA213 or BA215 and get a cable from him.

If you want the part number for the BA213 cable I can look
at my BA213 tonight.

The BA440 cab-kit for the KFQSA has a short DSSI cable
with two external connectors and one internal connector.  You
could try using that as a source for the external connector.
(The cable is much too short to use in the BA215.)

> If it works at all, I'd wager the drives are terminating the DSSI bus,
> but I'm only guessing.

I don't think the DSSI drives have terminators on them.  On my
cluster at home the 4000/100, 105A and 106A all fail the self
test if the bus isn't terminated.  My 3200, 3400  and 3800 don't
detect missing terminators.

Finding the correct DSSI cables was a major source of delay
for my hobbyist cluster!

Robert

