Hi,

Wartan Hachaturow wrote:
>
> Recently I've got a 164LX motherboard together with
> 533Mhz processor and 512Mb memory bank.
> Now, I'm in the midst of assembling a computer out of it ;)
> I'd like to run a Tru64 v5.1A along with Debian Linux on
> this machine -- but I fail to find a suitable hardware
> compatibilty list for the first -- Tru64.

The following parts should work for Tru64, OpenVMS and Linux:

> 1. Video card.

Elsa Gloria Synergy
Diamond Fire GL 1000 Pro

These cards are based on the Permedia 2 chip.
You could also get an older Trio64 based card, but sometimes
Tru64 seems to have problems. I had an Elsa Trio64 that
worked fine with VMS, but not with Tru64.

> This should be a PCI one. Will Matrox Millenium work with
> Tru64's X?

No.

> 2. Hard drive.

Anything SCSI.
IDE will not work with VMS. I'm not sure about Tru64.
For Tru64 you could get a Symbios Logic SCSI 875 controller.
For Tru64 _and_ VMS, get an NCR 810 based card.

> 3. Network card.

Difficult. With Linux you will have no problems at all.
For Tru64 you could try an old DECchip based card. I run a
modern 100Mbit card with Intel tulip chipset under VMS.
Maybe that works with Tru64 too.

> 4. Sound card.

I had an even older Soundblaster AWE 32 ISA card working
under Linux. These chipsets are supposed to work with Tru64
or VMS:

ESS 1888/7 (I think this is the PWS sound system)
Orchid NuSound
Ensoniq 1373 SB64 PCI (Important: 1370 doesn't work)
TC LoFI 
 
HTH
Dennis


