HD male connector so I can't neither terminate the DSSI bus nor build
a DSSI-based cluster with its neighbour, a 4000-200 (I've configured
the 3300 as a satellite of the 4000-200 via LAVC).

I'm trying to find someone here (Barcelona) capable of building a new
cable with the proper connector, but so far I've been out of luck
(everyone says "oh, this is SCSI"... and then look at me with a funny
face when I try to explain them what is a DSSI or, even worse, what is
a VAX... :)).

The cable has a paper label adhered. I think the DEC part # WAS
written on that label.Unfortunately it's not readable anymore.

So I'm asking:

- Anyone knows what is the DEC part # of this cable, or any compatible
one? I'll call the local DEC-Compaq reseller to ask for it...

- Anyone has a spare one to sell to me? ;) (This WOULD be a lot of
luck ;)).

