termination?  The "provisional" (so I hope) SCSI cable ends in a RF72
drive. I've read somewhere that the RFxx drives CAN terminate a DSSI
bus, but I guess there is some dip switch or jumper to set...

I'm not very good drawing ASCII, but here is my try for this cable:

    E-------C------C------C

The "E" is a male HD50 pin connector, which is fixed to the DSSI
"external" port.

The C are standard 2x25 female connectors. The one at the right side
plugs into a male connector fixed by a pair of screws to the metal
case which separates the TK70  bay from the HD area.

Any help will be apreciated.

