We carried the Alpha version forward as long as we could, certainly long
after it was dropped by nearly everybody else.  Ditto for the PowerPC
version before that.  Ditto for OS/2.  It's not that we enjoy dropping
things -- quite the opposite, as anybody can see who looks at the
platforms we DO support with C-Kermit, for example.  It's that newer
versions of K95 become unbuildable on older platforms for all sorts of
reasons.  In the case of K95, it's usually that libraries that we need to
link with -- e.g.  OpenSSL 0.9.7 -- are not available for those platforms.
Or that the hardware where we do the builds has died.  Or some other
impediment that would cost us serious time or money to overcome.

As long as we can do the builds without encountering serious roadblocks,
we do them.

