Well, so far you have scored "Null Points"

1) Video card there are very few choices that work and are supported
    i) VX1 Oxygen 32MB PCI Video Card
    ii) S3Trio64 PCi (not very good res)
   iii) Permedia 2 Based PCI Card (not Permedia 2V) like the ELSA GLoria
       (We sell a VMS/Tru64 compatible one for $149)

2) IDE will not work as a boot disk in your PC164LX board
    YOU MUST USE SCSI
     You cannot use an Adaptec controller
      It MUST be either a Qlogic QLA1020(a), QLogic QLA1040b or LSI(Symbios)
      53C875 or 53C895
      Even then it can be touch and go whether it will work or not based on
card firmware

3) Network cards need to be based on the 21140/21143 DEC Chip
    Newer cards with Intel part numbers are around also but I can't remember
the chip ID
4)  Sound card - ESS 1868 works - also 1869 based card and the Soundblaster
PCI 4610

Good luck

David


