:Ladies and Gents,
:I recently acquired two DEC 2000 AXP (Jensens).  I have a bunch of 4.3
:GB SCSI-2 Hard disks that I would like to throw in them, but they
:always cause the SCSI bus to reset and time out when installing. 
:These drives are Seagate Barracuda's ST34371N.  Do the drives need a
:special firmware to work in an alpha, is there any way to get them to
:work?

  The DEC 2000 series is unfortunately rather difficult to deal with, 
  largely arising from its status as the first EISA-based Alpha system.

  Please scan the archives for the various existing discussions of 
  the SCSI on the DEC 2000 series Jensen.  

  There are no special firmware requirements in the SCSI drives, but 
  you have to be EXCEEEEEEEEEDINGLY CAREFUL not to perturb the SCSI 
  configuration nor the SCSI timing, you cannot extend the internal 
  SCSI out of the box, and you must only use specific SCSI controllers. 
  Unlike the SCSI drives, there ARE firmware revision requirements for 
  the SCSI controllers used in this system.  (Again, see the archives.)

  For general information on SCSI and on third-party SCSI widgets and 
  on OpenVMS ECO kits, please see the OpenVMS FAQ.


