You can use a Windows NT V4.0 Server as a TCP/IP Boot Host for all of the
Digital PrintServer printers, with the exception of a PrintServer 20. The
processor in the PrintServers is a MicroVAX and the PrintServer is plugged
into a network, on powerup it emits a MOP request for a boot load from an
appropriately configured host. The downloaded file is VAXELN code that
speaks DECnet and TCP/IP. I am afraid that I have not much more ot add to
that other than much of the actual information about setup is in WIndows NT
V4,0 and also available on the internet.

http://www1.sqp.com/MasterIndex/installation_guide_011bb09c.txt has an
OpenVMS guide, that has informative diatribe.

